# Cell from playpick: mode=menus, view=820x1180,touch, save=carried.
#
# What no session has done before: direction.md's 2026-09-30 entry reads
# `src/main.ts`'s `encounter` variable as the mechanism behind "escaping a
# daily fight leaves the roster screen's own banner naming the daily's
# boss" -- it is only ever reset by the raid *setup* screen's own NEXT press
# (`updateRaidSetup`, main.ts:1841-1844), never by an escape, and the entry
# calls the bug general to "any fight escaped without going through raid
# setup first." But every session that touched it only ever escaped
# straight back to that one stale roster and read the label once. Grepped
# direction.md/sessions.jsonl for "battleground" next to "escape"/"roster":
# zero hits, and grepped src/main.ts for "encounter =" near any battleground
# code: no matches -- a battleground never assigns to the variable.
# Prediction going in: playing and escaping a battleground in between does
# not wash the stale daily-boss label out, since nothing on that path
# touches `encounter`.
#
# Real control names found first via -6-probe.play rather than guessed.
# Also discovered live, this run: `back` from the post-escape `roster`
# screen lands on the raid *size/difficulty* screen, not home directly --
# a second `back` is needed, and that screen's own `next` is the only thing
# in the game that resets `encounter`, so this script stops one press short
# of it to keep the staleness alive for the battleground half of the test.
open
tap daily
tap class:0
tap start
waitscreen fight 15
wait 3
key Escape
shot roster-daily-fresh

tap back
tap back
tap battleground
tap map:conquest
shot roster-bg-fresh

tap pull
waitscreen fight 15
play mash 20
shot bg-mid
state

key Escape
targets
state
shot roster-after-bg-escape
